# Agents & workflows

**Skald** is Wyrd's agent runtime. Where cards *describe* components, Skald *runs*
the agentic ones. You define an agent — its tools, its prompt, its provider — once,
and run it from **Python or Rust** with full parity. Workflows compose agents into
sequential or parallel pipelines.

<Aside title="Define once, run in either language" data-variant="wyrd">

The same agent and workflow surface ships in Python and Rust. Pick the language
that fits your stack; the run loop, tools, providers, and structured output behave
identically.

</Aside>

## The pieces

- **Agent** — a model-backed loop with a system prompt, a set of tools, and a
  provider. Running it returns an `AgentRun` with the result and the turn-by-turn
  trace.
- **Tools** — plain functions the agent can call. In Python you mark them with
  `@tool`; the runtime resolves them by name through its tool registry.
- **Prompt** — the instructions the agent runs under. Author prompts inline, or
  register a [Prompt card](/cards/prompt/) and hand it to the agent so the prompt
  you versioned is the prompt that runs.
- **Provider** — where the model lives. Skald ships OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini,
  Vertex, and a Mock provider, plus a gateway for routing.
- **Workflow** — agents composed `sequential` or `parallel`, with handoff between
  steps and typed structured output.

## The run loop

An agent run is the familiar loop: the model receives the prompt and the available
tools, decides whether to call a tool, the runtime executes the tool and feeds the
result back, and the loop continues until the model returns a final answer. Skald
owns that loop, the provider wire formats, tool dispatch, and the trace; your code
owns the tools and the prompt.

## Providers

Configure a provider with its credentials (typically an environment variable per
provider) and name it when you build the agent. The **Mock** provider needs no
credentials and is the right choice for tests and examples — it returns scripted
responses so a run is deterministic.

| Provider | Backend |
|---|---|
| OpenAI | OpenAI Chat / Responses APIs |
| Anthropic | Anthropic Messages API |
| Gemini | Google Gemini API |
| Vertex | Google Vertex AI |
| Mock | Deterministic, no credentials — for tests |

